{"step_index":245,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T15:22:41Z","thinking":"The model confidently classifies `scratch_00023.png` as \"scratch\" with 100% confidence. Considering the high accuracy, examining image dimensions and features of both `scratch_00023.png` and a similar image, `rust_00023.png`, is crucial to understand the characteristics that differentiate these defect types. Reviewing the standard characteristics of the dataset is necessary to build a correct intuition.\n\n\nThe current approach of a bounding box for images with pervasive defects may be misleading; the classification, based on global image features, is better visualized without arbitrary highlighting. A cleaner presentation, like a status badge and confidence meter, provides the most helpful information for the user without distorting the original data. The option for saliency maps could enhance the user's understanding of the classifier's focus.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"YOLOv8 inference wrapper with clean HUD annotation, Grad-CAM Heatmaps, and probability breakdown.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport os\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import Optional\\n\\nimport cv2\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport torch\\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw, ImageFont\\n\\nfrom utils.constants import (\\n    DEFECT_CLASSES,\\n    DEFECT_COLORS,\\n    STATUS_COLORS,\\n    CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD,\\n    NOVEL_THRESHOLD,\\n    MODEL_PATHS,\\n)\\n\\ntry:\\n    from ultralytics import YOLO\\n    _YOLO_AVAILABLE = True\\nexcept ImportError:\\n    _YOLO_AVAILABLE = False\\n\\n_model_cache: dict[str, object] = {}\\n\\n\\n# ── Model Loading ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\ndef load_model(custom_path: Optional[str] = None) -> tuple[object | None, str | None]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return (model, error_msg). Model is cached per path.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not _YOLO_AVAILABLE:\\n        return None, (\\n            \\\"ultralytics not installed.\\\\n\\\"\\n            \\\"Run: pip install ultralytics\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n    search_paths = ([custom_path] if custom_path else []) + MODEL_PATHS\\n    for path in search_paths:\\n        if not path:\\n            continue\\n        if path in _model_cache:\\n            return _model_cache[path], None\\n        if os.path.exists(path):\\n            try:\\n                model = YOLO(path)\\n                _model_cache[path] = model\\n                return model, None\\n            except Exception as exc:\\n                return None, f\\\"Failed to load {path}: {exc}\\\"\\n\\n    checked = [p for p in search_paths if p]\\n    return None, (\\n        f\\\"Model weights not found.\\\\n\\\"\\n        f\\\"Checked:\\\\n\\\" + \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(f\\\"  • {p}\\\" for p in checked) +\\n        \\\"\\\\n\\\\nPlace best.pt at D:\\\\\\\\acceleration\\\\\\\\best.pt or upload below.\\\"\\n    )\\n\\n\\n# ── PyTorch Grad-CAM Neural Activation ──────────\n<truncated 12400 bytes>","Description":"\"Clean industrial HUD annotation without fake boxes by default, plus Grad-CAM heatmaps and optional boxes mode\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\win-10\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\neurax_app\\\\modules\\\\defect_detector.py\"","toolAction":"\"Updating defect detector\"","toolSummary":"\"Clean HUD and multiple view modes\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
